<title>USA: Exxon says Calif. refinery at full capacity.</title>
<headline>Exxon says Calif. refinery at full capacity.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Exxon Corp said on Wednesday its 135,000 barrel-per-day (bpd) refinery in Benecia, Calif., ran at full capacity, following planned maintenance shutdowns of several processing units this winter.</p>
<p>&quot;The refinery is operating normally,&quot; said a Exxon spokesman. &quot;All units are up and running. They were all back as of yesterday,&quot; he said.  </p>
<p>The restarted units include a 26,000 bpd coking unit, a 29,000 bpd hydrocracking unit and vacuum pipestill, all of which shut between late January and early February.</p>
<p>((David Brinkerhoff, Los Angeles bureua +1 213 380 2014))</p>
